{
  "key": "gh-1206",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[BENCH] jupyter-notebook-server: test_timeout with the agent's work done — test budget too tight for slow-start server tasks",
    "description": "TBench-1 rerun 37144207185 (2026-10-03, glm-5.3-flash): **jupyter-notebook-server** ended `failure_mode=test_timeout` while the agent's pane shows the job DONE — server up, password configured («Logs at /app/jupyter.log. Tests can authenticate with password benchmarkpass.»). The verifier tests blew THEIR time budget, not the agent's.

Slow-start services (jupyter, databases) burn tens of seconds on first boot; the test budget doesn't account for it.

**Fix**: raise/pad the test-timeout knob for server-class tasks in the bench harness (the #1122 knob family covers agent caps; add/pad the test side), or add a readiness-wait before the test clock starts. Evidence: /tmp/bench3/shard-*/jupyter-notebook-server (run 37144207185, shard 2 or 5).

